Orbital Laser, Fabric port
==========================

Copyright (c) 2026 Ramingen, MIT License (see LICENSE).

A port to Minecraft Java Edition on the Fabric loader of Orbital Laser (https://github.com/Stink-O/orbital-laser,
Copyright (c) 2026 Stink-O, MIT License). The port is by Ramingen. It is released under the same MIT License, as the
original's licence requires, and LICENSE keeps Stink-O's copyright notice beside Ramingen's.

An independent fan project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Mojang Studios, Microsoft, or the author of Orbital
Laser. Minecraft is a trademark and work of Mojang Studios and Microsoft. Nothing from Minecraft is in this repository: no
game code (decompiled or otherwise), textures, sounds or data. The mod is built against the game, Fabric Loader and Fabric
API, which Gradle downloads when you build it; none of them is included.

What comes from Orbital Laser
-----------------------------

src/main/java            Written for this port. Its strike plans (Plan, StandardPlan, MeteorPlan, MothershipPlan,
                         BigPlans, ShaderTables, Rng, Laser) follow the original's Rust (mod/src/lasers.rs, strike.rs,
                         strike/*.rs): the same numbers, timelines and random-number generator. BigPlans is a simplified
                         port of the Planet Killer, Downfall, Crystal Bloom, Sinkhole, Payload (world changes) and Nuke
                         (world changes).
src/main/resources/assets/orbital
                         Items, models, textures, names, sounds.json and sounds, copied from the original's
                         orbital-laser-mod/ and orbital-sounds/. The sounds are synthesized from noise and tones by the
                         original's tools/synth_sounds.py and contain no samples from any recording; the item textures are
                         drawn by its tools/make_item_textures.py.
src/client/resources/assets/orbital/shaders/post
                         strike.fsh, payload.fsh and nuke.fsh are GLSL translations, made by tools/build_shader.py, of the
                         original's mod/shaders/strike.wgsl, payload.wgsl and nuke.wgsl (MIT). They are generated files:
                         regenerate them with the tools, do not edit them. strike.vsh is a full-screen triangle written for
                         this port.

Third-party material
--------------------

tools/wgsl2glsl
  A small program that links naga (MIT or Apache-2.0, https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu) to translate WGSL to GLSL. naga is
  downloaded by cargo when you build the tool; it is not included.

gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar, gradlew, gradlew.bat
  The Gradle wrapper (Apache License 2.0, https://gradle.org), as generated by the Fabric example mod template.

build.gradle, settings.gradle, gradle.properties, .github/workflows/build.yml
  Adapted from the Fabric example mod (https://github.com/FabricMC/fabric-example-mod, CC0 1.0).
